  "title": "The prototype chain",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Shared methods live on the prototype\n\n`Object.getPrototypeOf(obj)` is the next place JS looks for a field. Many objects share one method object. That is `[[Prototype]]`, not a copy of the function on every instance.\n\nTwo foxes from the same prototype share one `go` function.\n\nThe desk does not copy `move` onto every route card. Each card looks up `go` on the shared prototype when you call it."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "shared-method",
      "promptMd": "Two objects from the same prototype share…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "own",
          "md": "A private copy of each method"
        },
        {
          "id": "one",
          "md": "One method function on the prototype"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "one"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "proto-share",
      "kind": "cloze",
      "promptMd": "Two objects from one prototype share {{a}}.",
      "blanks": [
